### **1. Mathematical Formulation & Code Location**

Under the Naive Bayes assumption of conditionally independent sensor channels given the hypothesis ($H_1 = \text{survivor}$, $H_0 = \text{no survivor}$), evidence is accumulated in **log-odds space**:

$$\text{log-odds}_{\text{posterior}} = \text{log-odds}_{\text{prior}} + \sum_{i \in \{\text{camera}, \text{audio}, \text{passive}\}} \ln \left( \frac{P(r_i \mid H_1)}{P(r_i \mid H_0)} \right)$$

$$P(H_1 \mid r_{\text{cam}}, r_{\text{aud}}, r_{\text{pass}}) = \sigma(\text{log-odds}_{\text{posterior}}) = \frac{1}{1 + e^{-\text{log-odds}_{\text{posterior}}}}$$

