The True Positive (`trueRate`), False Positive (`falseRate`), and Likelihood Ratio (`LR`) calculations are located in two places across the frontend and backend:

---

### **1. Frontend: [`src/uncertainty.js`](file:///c:/Users/Punit%20Raveendran/Desktop/Projects/Drone-DSU/src/uncertainty.js#L84-L126)**

#### **A. The Likelihood Ratio Engine (`channelLogLR`)**
* **Lines 84–95 in [`src/uncertainty.js`](file:///c:/Users/Punit%20Raveendran/Desktop/Projects/Drone-DSU/src/uncertainty.js#L84-L95)**:
```javascript
function channelLogLR(reading, trueRate, falseRate) {
  if (reading < NOISE_FLOOR) {
    // Below noise floor: weak negative evidence (absence of evidence)
    return Math.log((1 - trueRate) / (1 - falseRate));
  }
  // Above noise floor: Likelihood Ratio P(reading|survivor) / P(reading|no_survivor)
  const pGivenSurvivor   = trueRate * reading + (1 - trueRate) * 0.05;
  const pGivenNoSurvivor = falseRate * reading + (1 - falseRate) * 0.05;
  return Math.log(pGivenSurvivor / pGivenNoSurvivor);
}
```

#### **B. The Channel-Specific True & False Positive Rates**
* **Lines 118–126 in [`src/uncertainty.js`](file:///c:/Users/Punit%20Raveendran/Desktop/Projects/Drone-DSU/src/uncertainty.js#L118-L126)**:
```javascript
// Camera (YOLOv8): Sensitivity = 85% (0.85), False Positive = 8% (0.08)
logOdds += channelLogLR(camera, 0.85, 0.08);

// Audio (YAMNet): Sensitivity = 80% (0.80), False Positive = 15% (0.15)
logOdds += channelLogLR(audio, 0.80, 0.15);

// Thermal / Gas (Passive): Sensitivity = 70% (0.70), False Positive = 30% (0.30)
logOdds += channelLogLR(passive, 0.70, 0.30);
```

